course: dictionary
lesson: 11774
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, look at the words around it. Those words are the context, and they give you clues.
explain: «Sam was batting when the ball flew over the fence for six.» Sam is in a game and hitting a ball, so batting means the turn to hit and score. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: The same word can work in a very different way. «The cat was batting at the moth with its paw.» Here batting is a verb, and it means hitting something with a paw. Look at the other words, like cat and moth, to know which meaning is right.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Batting» can be a noun (a turn in a game) or the -ing form of the verb «bat» (hitting something).
fact: In cricket and baseball, batting is the turn when your team tries to score by hitting the ball.
fact: «Batting» also means a layer of soft cotton or wool inside a quilt, and «to bat your eyelashes» means to blink them quickly.
fact: A «batting order» is the order in which players take their turn to bat.
exercise: «Sam was batting when the ball flew over the fence for six.» What is batting here? | Hitting a friend with his hand | Blinking his eyes quickly | Covering a bed with soft cotton | *Hitting a ball with a bat for his team's turn to score
exercise: «The cat was batting at the moth with its paw.» What is the cat doing? | Sleeping on a soft quilt | Counting the moths in the room | Singing to the moth | *Hitting at the moth with its paw
exercise: «Lily said the quilt had a thick batting of soft cotton inside.» What is batting in the quilt? | A game played with a bat | A quick blink of the eyes | A ball thrown very fast | *A layer of soft cotton or wool
test: «Tom was batting his eyelashes quickly because the sun was bright.» What does batting his eyelashes mean? | Painting them black | Closing them for a long sleep | *Blinking them quickly | Hitting them with a bat
test: «In cricket, the team that is batting first scores runs.» What does batting mean here? | Bowling the ball very fast | *Taking the turn to hit the ball and score runs | Running away from the ball | Catching the ball in the field
exam: «She listened to the loud crash without batting an eyelid.» What does without batting an eyelid mean? | Closing her eyes tightly | *Showing no surprise at all | Jumping up in fright | Starting to cry
